The reasoning improperly broadens quantifiers. It moves from "duo is South Korean" (a group-level property) to "both members must be from South Korea" (an individual-level universal claim). This assumes that "South Korean duo" inherently means "duo composed entirely of South Koreans," which is an unstated and questionable assumption.

